>> title: Potato Salad
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: potato, mayonnaise, mustard, cold, side
>> counters: Meat and Three, Smokehouse, Deli
>> aka: southern potato salad, mustard potato salad, cold potato salad, tater salad
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr 35 min
>> pairs-with: coleslaw, fried-chicken, smoked-brisket, barbecue-slaw
>> step.1: Toss the potatoes while they are still hot enough to steam. Cold potatoes take on nothing at all, and the whole difference between a good bowl and a bland one is when the dressing goes on.
>> step.2: boil 14 min, drain dry
>> step.3: whisk the dressing
>> step.4: toss warm
>> step.5: fold the cold things through
>> step.6: chill 2 hr

Toss the potatoes while they are still hot enough to steam. Cold potatoes take on nothing at all, and the whole difference between a good bowl and a bland one is when the dressing goes on.

Boil @Yukon Gold potatoes{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 1-in chunks) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs} for ~boil{14%min}.

Whisk @mayonnaise{1%cup}(220 g), @yellow mustard{3%Tbs}, @cider vinegar{2%Tbs}, @granulated sugar{2%tsp}, @celery seed{1/2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}.

Toss @&(~2)drained potatoes{} warm through @&(~1)mustard dressing{}.

Fold @&(~1)dressed potatoes{} with @hard-boiled eggs{4}(chopped), @celery{2%ribs}(finely diced), @sweet pickle relish{1/4%cup}(60 g), @red onion{1/2%small}(minced).

Chill @&(~1)potato salad{} for ~chill{2%hr}.

Season it again once it is cold. Chilling flattens the salt and the vinegar both, and a bowl seasoned only while warm arrives at the table tasting of nothing much.
